+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-add-create-patch/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+## Why
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document. The library can apply an RFC 6902 patch but cannot produce one.
+
+## What Changes
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 patch that `applyPatch` turns from `from` into `to`.
+- The patch is a minimal-style diff: it recurses into objects and arrays and emits operations only for the parts that changed.
+- Neither input is mutated.
+
+## Capabilities
+### New Capabilities
+None.
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: adds patch generation.
+
+## Impact
+`src/index.ts`, `README.md`, tests.
